  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nIssued 318 PM MDT WED JUL 15 2026\nThe region will remain on the western edge of a hot upper level \nridge through the period. After a break from the deeper monsoon \nmoisture over the weekend, the chance of showers and thunderstorms \nwill expand over the area early next week. Higher terrain in \nsouthwest Idaho zones will be the focus development while southeast \nOregon is positioned on the fringe of the deeper moisture. The water \ncontent of the air mass will again reach the +95th percentile as \nprecipitable water values are forecast to surpass 1.20 inches. This \nwould certainly favor heavy rainmakers. Temperatures will remain \nabove normal with lower elevations seeing highs near 100 while dew \npoints in the 50s to low 60s will increase the humidity early next \nweek.",
